@participant40 

That's another issue. Typed Routes are enabled in your config under the `experimental` flag. It provides route suggestions based on the routes you've defined, based on the file system and also based on the routes you've defined in your `_layout` files. I've disabled mine for now because I know the structure of my routes and I know what params they take. It was a nice addition, but since it is experimental I tend to not care much when it breaks, I simply just disable it. You can learn more from [here](https://docs.expo.dev/router/reference/typed-routes/)


As for your issue, since you are using Expo, you can customize your Expo Menu when you press `M` in your terminal or shake it. So as a start to see what is going on, I suggest you to create this hook:

```ts
import { useRouter } from "expo-router";
import { useEffect } from "react";
import { registerDevMenuItems } from "expo-dev-menu";

export const useDevRoutes = () => {
  const router = useRouter();

  useEffect(() => {
    const devMenuItems = [
      {
        name: `Go to Sitemap`,
        callback: () => router.push("/_sitemap"),
      },
    ];

    registerDevMenuItems(devMenuItems);
  }, [router]);
};
```

Put it in your root `_layout` file and run it like usual.

Now when you press `M` to open up the dev menu, You will see a new a menu item called `Go to Sitemap` and when you press it, it shows all the registered routes there. And try to see what your `LocationScreen` component is registered as. Let me know if you found the problem and if it is related to typed routes at all. Have a good day.

